Yes. If you want to run a Python script while tcpdump is capturing network traffic, using two Ubuntu terminal sessions is the easiest approach.

### Session 1: Run tcpdump

bash
sudo tcpdump -i any -w capture.pcap


This continuously captures packets and saves them into capture.pcap.

### Session 2: Run your Python script

bash
python3 script.py


Your Python script can generate network traffic, while tcpdump captures it simultaneously.

### Session 3 (optional): Analyse captured traffic

bash
tcpdump -r capture.pcap


Or use:

bash
tshark -r capture.pcap


### How the setup works

Terminal 1

tcpdump — captures packets

Terminal 2

Python — generates test traffic

Terminal 3 (optional)

TShark — analyses saved packets

You only need two sessions for capturing and running Python simultaneously. The third is optional. Use a network you own or have permission to test.
